  "section_notes": "The final v24 sets a hard 5% per-model failure cap with no transition, which effectively bars Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%) until it retests, while per-model results go to regulators and customers but not to the public. The S5 mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 has no transition, so Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) would fall under it, and the S3 six-year retrofit window favours Northwind's low shut-off coverage. The S3 new-unit deadline of 24 months and the S2 customer-disclosure wording (model-specific results, read here as numeric) are the main interpretive points."
